 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No well, bucket, caravan, sale, coins or boy drawn (19-20 have no plate). 19:11-16 is not glossed (who hid him is disputed). A house for «أكرمي مثواه», a book for «تأويل الأحاديث» (after Yusuf's name), geometric for «والله غالب على أمره», light for «آتيناه حكما وعلما». 21:15-19 and 22:4-6 are not glossed (first person). STAGING v4: c1 (19-20): a caravan in the desert by day (As-Sa'di: a caravan heading for Egypt): three travellers and a camel walk in (19:1), they send their water drawer (a man with a traveller's staff, 19:3) who walks to the left (19:4) and calls out the good news to them (19:7); Yusuf, a blue drop labelled Yusuf, appears beside him on this is a boy (19:9). The well, the bucket and the lifting are never drawn; Yusuf is never shown as a captive, nothing is drawn for they hid him. Geometric for Allah knows what they do (19:13-16). The sale is shown only by a small coins plate (20:2-5): no purse is handed over, nobody counts, the brothers are not drawn. No close-up, pan or glow on the drop. c2 (21-22) stays ambient (light): al-Aziz speaks to his wife (21:1-14), so nobody is drawn; then Allah's acts for Yusuf (We established him, We taught him, We gave him judgement and knowledge): the background stays quiet over 21:15-27 and 22:4-9. Plates as before, except light now starts on judgement (22:5), not on We gave him (a pronoun of Allah). Cover: the caravan arriving in the desert (title: from the well to Egypt)."
 },
